Describe the agent 'Invoicing Agent' as a manifest. It is a pro-tier operations agent for the africa market. Africa Invoicing Agent for Highveld Joinery Johannesburg (Johannesburg) — localized production pack with confirm-before-write and human handoff.
It runs on whatsapp, web, app in en. Compliance: popia, regional_privacy. Human handoff triggers: dispute, tax_or_advice, explicit_request, low_confidence.
Tools:
- get_invoice: Look up a single invoice by its number and return its amount, dates and payment status. Read-only; use this for any specific invoice query rather than quoting figures from the knowledge base.
- list_invoice_templates: List the invoice templates the business has set up so you can offer the owner a choice before creating an invoice. Read-only; call this rather than naming template ids from memory.
- create_invoice: Raise a new invoice for a customer from the given line items, optionally on a chosen template. Use only after you have read the customer, line items and total back to the owner and they have confirmed; this creates a customer-facing document, so it is never called on the first turn without a clear yes.
- send_invoice: Email an existing invoice to the customer. Use only after confirming the recipient with the owner; this sends a document, so it is never called on the first turn without a clear yes.
- record_payment: Record a payment a customer has made against an invoice. Financial action: use only after reading the amount, date and payment mode back to the owner and getting a clear yes. This only records a payment the owner says was received — it never moves money or takes a payment.
- list_outstanding_invoices: List every invoice that still has money owing (sent, overdue, or part-paid), with each one's balance and due date. Read-only; use this to answer 'what's outstanding', 'which invoices are unpaid or overdue', or 'who owes us' rather than guessing. Present the results as a short list with amounts and offer to send a reminder on any of them.
- send_reminder: Email a payment reminder to the customer for an outstanding invoice, by invoice number. This sends a real email to the customer, so state which invoice (and, if given, which address) and get a clear yes from the owner before calling it. Use for overdue or unpaid invoices surfaced by list_outstanding_invoices or get_invoice.
- get_aging_summary: Summarise everything still owing, bucketed by how overdue it is (not yet due, 1-30, 31-60, 60+ days), with a total. Read-only; use this for 'who owes us', 'what's our aging', or a debtor overview. Present the buckets with amounts and offer to send reminders on the overdue ones.
- find_customer: Look up a customer by name to get their id and email, so you can raise or reconcile an invoice for them. Read-only. Use this when the owner names a customer but you don't have their id yet; if several match, ask which one.
- create_customer: Add a new customer to the accounting system so you can invoice them. Confirm the name (and email, if given) with the owner before calling. Returns the new customer id to use with create_invoice.
- mark_invoice_sent: Move a draft invoice to Sent status WITHOUT emailing the customer, so a payment can be recorded against it (Zoho won't accept a payment on a draft). Confirm with the owner first. Use this when the owner wants to record a payment on an invoice that is still a draft, or wants it marked sent without emailing.
- get_invoice_link: Get the customer-facing shareable link (and view/pay page) for an invoice so the owner can forward it. Read-only. Use when the owner asks for the link, the PDF, or to 'send me' / 'share' an invoice.
- create_payment_link: Generate a Paystack 'pay now' link for an outstanding invoice so the customer can pay by card/EFT online. Give the invoice number — the link is created for that invoice's outstanding balance, in ZAR, with the invoice number as the payment reference. Confirm with the owner before sending the link to a customer. Share the returned link; never take card details in chat.

