Describe the agent 'Clinic Front Desk' as a manifest. It is a pro-tier vertical agent. A non-clinical front desk — books appointment requests, shares preparation instructions and practice basics, and hands every clinical or emergency question straight to a human, across WhatsApp, web and app.
It runs on whatsapp, web, app in en, af, zu. Human handoff triggers: clinical_question, emergency, explicit_request, low_confidence.
Tools:
- list_services: List the practice's non-clinical services with durations and prices. Use when a patient asks what the practice offers or what something costs. Read-only.
- check_availability: Find open appointment times for a service on a given date. Always call this before offering any time. Read-only.
- book_appointment: Capture a confirmed appointment request into an open slot. Only call after the patient has confirmed service, date & time, name and contact, and only for a slot that check_availability returned. Returns a booking reference. This is an administrative booking, not a clinical assessment.
- get_prep_instructions: Return the practice's preparation instructions for a booked procedure (logistics only — e.g. fasting time, what to bring). Not medical advice. Use when a patient asks how to prepare for a specific procedure. Read-only.
- handoff_to_human: Route the conversation to a human (reception or a clinician) with a summary and recent context. Use for ANY clinical or symptom question, any emergency, an explicit request for a person, or the agent's own low confidence, so the patient does not have to repeat themselves.

